WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.864 --> 00:00:12.573
In this walkthrough, we create a subpage from a parent row in the page tree. The example parent is Venue and travel, but the same pattern works for any parent page.

2
00:00:12.573 --> 00:00:20.036
This is useful because it shows the path through the admin interface before you need to do the same task on real content.

3
00:00:20.036 --> 00:00:26.013
Start on the Pages screen. This is where parent and child pages are managed.

4
00:00:26.013 --> 00:00:31.940
Search for the parent page first, so the row you need is visible even in a large page tree.

5
00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:37.170
Confirm that the parent page row is visible before you use its row actions.

6
00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:44.819
Click the add child page action on that parent row. This is the step that makes the new page a subpage.

7
00:00:44.819 --> 00:00:51.677
The new page form opens from that parent, so the child relationship is carried into the page you are about to create.

8
00:00:51.677 --> 00:00:55.191
Enter a clear title for the subpage.

9
00:00:55.191 --> 00:01:00.097
Check the slug because it becomes part of the URL path below Venue and travel.

10
00:01:00.097 --> 00:01:08.027
Click Create Page to create the subpage. Tutorial recordings use demo data, so this does not create real production content.

11
00:01:08.027 --> 00:01:13.629
Before publishing, check that the page path and navigation area match the parent you selected.

12
00:01:13.629 --> 00:01:24.153
After this walkthrough, you should know how to find the parent page, create the child page, and confirm that the new page belongs under the right parent before publishing.
